OpenCASCADE Technology (OCCT)
-----------------------------
crates/kernel-occt calls OpenCASCADE Technology 8, Copyright (c) Open CASCADE SAS, licensed under
the GNU Lesser General Public License version 2.1 with the Open CASCADE Exception 1.0
(https://dev.opencascade.org/resources/licensing). OCCT is NOT part of this repository and is not
compiled into Tenon: it is linked dynamically as shared libraries (TKernel, TKMath, TKBRep, ...).

- Obtaining the source: the exact OCCT version used is pinned in pixi.toml and pixi.lock (the
  conda-forge "occt" package). Its source is available from
  https://github.com/Open-Cascade-SAS/OCCT and from the conda-forge feedstock
  https://github.com/conda-forge/occt-feedstock.
- Replacing it: build any compatible OCCT 8.0.x yourself and point Tenon at it, either by setting
  OCCT_ROOT to its install prefix when building, or by replacing the shared libraries next to a
  packaged Tenon binary (DLLs on Windows, .so on Linux, .dylib on macOS). No relinking of Tenon is
  needed for a binary-compatible OCCT.
- Rebuilding Tenon against a modified OCCT: the complete source of Tenon is available in this
  repository; `OCCT_ROOT=/your/occt cargo build --release` relinks it (docs/setup.md).

The C++ shim in crates/kernel-occt/shim is original Tenon code (MIT OR Apache-2.0) written against
OCCT's public headers.

Gmsh and CalculiX
-----------------
Stress studies are worked out by two programs that are NOT part of this repository, are not
linked into Tenon and are not shipped with it: Gmsh (Copyright (c) C. Geuzaine and J.-F. Remacle,
GNU General Public License version 2 or later, https://gmsh.info) and CalculiX (Copyright (c)
Guido Dhondt, GNU General Public License version 2, http://www.dhondt.de). Tenon starts them as
separate programs and exchanges files with them (docs/stress.md). pixi.toml names them so that a
developer can download them from conda-forge into an environment of their own; whoever passes
either program on to others does so under that program's licence. Nothing in Tenon is derived
from their source: the readers and writers of their file formats in crates/fea are original
Tenon code.

